THOUGHT: The field `spawnpoints` is annotated `@Nullable`, but `getSpawnPoints()` must return a non-null `List<Spawnpoint>` (per the interface and NullAway). The safest fix is to ensure the getter never returns null by lazily initializing `spawnpoints` to an empty list when it’s null. This avoids changing interface annotations and prevents NPEs where `getSpawnPoints()` is used (e.g., `.isEmpty()`, `.size()`). After changing the method, I should run the compile task to confirm the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '104,106c\  @Override
  public List<Spawnpoint> getSpawnPoints() {
    if (this.spawnpoints == null) {
      this.spawnpoints = new ArrayList<>();
    }

    return this.spawnpoints;
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/environment/EntitySpawner.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "EntitySpawner.java" new_build_output.log || true
```

